<Project>
    <PropertyGroup>
        <!-- NuGet Package Info -->
        <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
        <PackageId>$(MSBuildProjectName)</PackageId>
        <Version>1.3.0</Version>
        <Authors>Andrea Ficarra</Authors>
        <Copyright>Copyright © 2026 Andrea Ficarra</Copyright>
        <Description>Lightweight, free, open-source in-process mediator for .NET. Supports requests, streaming requests, notifications, pipeline behaviors, pre/post-processors, exception handlers/actions, and pluggable notification sinks.</Description>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Adiakys/OpenMediator</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Adiakys/OpenMediator</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>
1.3.0:
- Add IRequestExceptionHandler&lt;TRequest, TResponse, TException&gt; (MediatR-compatible). Implementations may recover from exceptions thrown by the handler or any pipeline step by calling RequestExceptionHandlerState.SetHandled with a fallback response. Multiple handlers per (request, exception) pair are supported and run in registration order until one marks the state as handled. Matches by exception type assignability so a handler for a base type catches derived exceptions.
- Add IRequestExceptionAction&lt;TRequest, TException&gt; (MediatR-compatible). Side-effects (logging, metrics, ...) triggered by an exception that has not been recovered. The original exception is always re-thrown after all matching actions complete; actions are skipped when an exception handler recovers via SetHandled.
- Add explicit registration via cfg.AddRequestExceptionHandler&lt;T&gt;() and cfg.AddRequestExceptionAction&lt;T&gt;(); the wrapper pipeline behaviors are wired automatically.
- Exception handlers and actions are auto-scanned from assemblies unconditionally (no opt-in flag), mirroring MediatR.
        </PackageReleaseNotes>
        <PackageTags>mediator;cqrs;pipeline;notifications;request-response;streaming;messaging;dotnet;open-source</PackageTags>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
        
        <!-- Build and Publish Settings -->
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
        <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- Optional: Additional files for the NuGet package -->
        <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
        <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
        <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)\..\icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
